# Draven voice policy (JonBeatz)

## Default voices

| Priority | Engine | When |
|----------|--------|------|
| **Primary** | **Edge** `en-CA-LiamNeural` (same as Hermes Desktop) | Every allowed speak |
| **Fallback** | **OmniVoice** (dialed-in British male, CPU) | Only if Edge fails |

**OmniVoice is still installed** with your saved knobs in `.env.local`. To use it as primary again, see **Restore OmniVoice** in `.cursor/docs/VOICE-WORKFLOW.md`.

## When to speak (allowed)

| Trigger | Action |
|---------|--------|
| **Start Project** ritual (cold boot) | `npm run draven:speak -- "..."` once (greeting) |
| **End Project** ritual (day-end) | `npm run draven:speak -- "..."` once (short farewell) |
| Jon says **speak**, **say**, **talk this**, **read aloud** | `npm run draven:speak -- "<exact text>"` |
| Critical **Mem0 / stack errors** | Only if `DRAVEN_VOICE_ERRORS=1` (default on) |

## When NOT to speak

- **Open Project** / **Resume Session** — silent resume.
- **Close Project** / **Close Session** — silent handoff.
- **Never** read ordinary chat replies or summaries aloud.
- **Never** speak after `mem0:add`, `mem0:search`, or successful Mem0 recall.
- **Never** auto-speak Hermes Desktop / Telegram agent responses (`auto_tts: false` in Hermes config).
- **Never** start OmniVoice daemon at PC boot — only if Omni is primary or fallback fires; stop on End Project.

## Commands

```powershell
npm run draven:speak -- "text"              # Edge Liam (Omni fallback on failure)
npm run draven:speak -- -OmniOnly "text"    # force OmniVoice once (premium)
npm run draven:omni-daemon                  # only if using Omni as primary
npm run draven:omni-daemon -- -Stop         # free RAM (also runs on session:stop)
```

`jarvis:*` aliases deprecated — use `draven:*` equivalents.

See **`.cursor/docs/VOICE-WORKFLOW.md`** for restore steps, errors, and resource notes.
